{
  "_comment": "Theme taxonomy for the Themes tiles page. This file is a MIRROR of the project's .fp/extensions/labels vocabulary: every theme 'key' must equal a label value, or that label can never win over keyword inference. fp ships no label vocabulary by default, so on a stock project every tile is keyword-inferred — see the README section 'The Themes page is only as good as your fp extensions'. Each issue's theme is resolved PER FACET in descending order of trust: (1) an explicit fp label matching a theme key (ties broken by the order themes appear here), (2) inherited from its epic — this outranks the issue's own keywords on purpose, so one initiative stays in one tile instead of fragmenting, (3) a weighted keyword match on title + description, which is how epics and standalone issues get classified, (4) 'unthemed'. Tiles count LEAF work items and partition them exactly; epics are reported separately, since an epic's status is a roll-up of its children. 'color' takes the same semantic names as the status registry (neutral/grey/blue/indigo/purple/teal/mint/green/amber/orange/red) or a raw #hex / var(--x). 'strong'/'weak' are case-insensitive regex fragments, OR-ed together; a title hit scores 6 (strong) / 3 (weak), a description hit 2 / 1. Best-scoring theme wins if it clears 'threshold' — raise it for fewer, more confident themes; lower it to leave less unthemed. A facet may override 'threshold' for its own themes.",
